# Eigen Project Rules and Guidelines

## Development Environment
1. Please don't run terminal commands to install packages yourself. Ask me to do it (so output the command and instructions as text)
2. Use Bun as the JavaScript runtime for both server and client development
3. All development should be done with TypeScript for type safety

## Project Overview
4. This is a Google Workspace-like application with multiple integrated apps (Mail, Drive, Docs, Calendar, Contacts, Space)
5. The project follows a monorepo structure with:
   - /apps: Contains all applications (frontend and API server)
   - /packages: Shared libraries and UI components
   - /packages/ui: Reusable UI components
   - /packages/lib: Shared business logic
   - /packages/config: Shared configuration

## Technical Stack
6. Backend: Bun + Elysia for server routes + Drizzle ORM for database
7. Frontend: React (with Bun) + TypeScript
8. Data Management: TanStack Query for data fetching and caching
9. Routing: TanStack Router for type-safe routing
10. UI: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui components
11. Authentication: better-auth for user authentication and session management

## Code Style & Conventions
12. ALWAYS USE ENGLISH in all code and all texts you generate
13. Prefer a simple and clean implementation. Keep code simple and HTML layout clean and simple
14. Use shadcn defaults for UI components
15. Follow established naming conventions:
    - For routes: Use domain-based naming (e.g., mail, drive, contacts)
    - For functions: Use camelCase and descriptive naming
    - For components: Use PascalCase

## Architecture Patterns
16. API Routes: Group by domain in /apps/api-server/src/routes
17. Frontend Apps: Place in separate directories under /apps
18. Shared Logic: Extract to /packages/lib
19. UI Components: Place reusable components in /packages/ui
20. Authentication: All protected routes should include the auth: true property

## Development Workflow
21. Use bun scripts defined in root package.json for development:
    - serve: Run all applications
    - serve:[appname]: Run specific app with API server
22. Always update types when changing database schemas
23. Remember to invalidate queries when mutating data
24. Create custom hooks for reusable data fetching logic

## State Management
25. Use TanStack Query for server state
26. Use React state hooks for local UI state
27. Use appropriate caching strategies for optimizing performance

## Documentation
28. Keep code comments minimal - code should be self-documenting:
    - DO NOT use JSDoc style comments
    - Only add comments to explain complex business logic that isn't immediately clear
    - Focus on making the code readable rather than relying on comments
    - Use clear variable and function names instead of comments where possible
29. Keep the README updated with setup instructions and project overview